  "narrative_text": "Three complementary pathway-analysis paradigms converge on a dominant biological signal: arachidonic acid metabolism and eicosanoid biosynthesis. RaMP-DB ORA identified Eicosanoid synthesis (WP:WP167) as the top pathway with FDR = 9.7e-14 (fold enrichment 1430, five input metabolites: 15-HETE, 5-HETE, 15-deoxy-d-12,14-PGJ2, arachidonic acid, leukotriene A4). Mummichog m/z-network analysis ranked Arachidonic acid metabolism (MUMM:arachidonic_acid_metabolism) first with p = 5.9e-4, mapping five input metabolites into a 13-member empirical network sub-module. MetaboAnalystR KEGG PSEA ranked hsa00590 first (arachidonic acid metabolism) with four metabolites hitting the pathway; 2-oxobutanoate (the anion form of 2-ketobutyric acid) independently hit valine pathway hsa00290 (p = 0.035). Glycerol and 4-hydroxybenzoic acid lacked pathway-level significance across all three tools. N-acetylgalactosamine was resolved to CHEBI:506227 (N-acetyl-D-glucosamine) by mummichog, with the KEGG C01074 annotation flagged for downstream reconciliation. No structural InChIKey conflicts were detected. Arachidonic acid is the primary substrate, bifurcating into the COX/PGJ2 branch and two LOX branches (5-LOX producing leukotriene A4 and 5-HETE; 15-LOX producing 15-HETE). 15-deoxy-PGJ2 signals PPARγ engagement. The 2-ketobutyric acid hit in hsa00290 (valine degradation) provides a minor but orthogonal metabolic node outside the lipid cascade.\n\nLimitations: N-acetylgalactosamine (KEGG:C01074) was annotated by mummichog as N-acetyl-D-glucosamine (KEGG:C00140) due to shared InChIKey first-block; this namespace ambiguity should be resolved before downstream interpretation. Glycerol and 4-hydroxybenzoic acid did not achieve pathway-level significance and may represent background noise or indirect metabolic effects.",
